p.src:
Let $V^\rho$ be transported along a curve. Parallel transport is defined by $\frac{D V^\rho}{Ds}
  =
  \frac{dV^\rho}{ds}
  +
  \Gamma^\rho{}_{\sigma\mu}V^\sigma
  \frac{dx^\mu}{ds}
  =0.$ For one infinitesimal displacement this becomes $dV^\rho
  =
  -\Gamma^\rho{}_{\sigma\mu}V^\sigma\,dx^\mu.$

