p.src:
We fix the convention $V^\rho
  =
  R^\rho{}_{\sigma\mu\nu}V^\sigma.$ With this convention, $\begin{aligned}
  R^\rho{}_{\sigma\mu\nu}
  &=
  \partial_\mu\Gamma^\rho{}_{\nu\sigma}
  -
  \partial_\nu\Gamma^\rho{}_{\mu\sigma}
  \nonumber\\
  &\quad
  +
  \Gamma^\rho{}_{\mu\lambda}
  \Gamma^\lambda{}_{\nu\sigma}
  -
  \Gamma^\rho{}_{\nu\lambda}
  \Gamma^\lambda{}_{\mu\sigma}.
  \end{aligned}$ Changing the order in the commutator or reversing the loop orientation changes the overall sign. Once a convention is declared, every later formula must follow it consistently.

