p.src:
In three dimensions the Riemann tensor contains no information beyond the Ricci tensor. Explicitly, $\begin{aligned}
  R_{abcd}
  &=
  g_{ac}R_{bd}-g_{ad}R_{bc}
  -g_{bc}R_{ad}+g_{bd}R_{ac}
  \nonumber\\
  &\quad
  -\frac{R}{2}
  \left(g_{ac}g_{bd}-g_{ad}g_{bc}\right).
  \end{aligned}$ In four dimensions this is no longer true; the Weyl tensor carries the remaining curvature information.

