p.src:
For a fixed volume $\Omega$, $\frac{d}{dt}\int_\Omega\rho_q\,d^3x
  =
  -\oint_{\partial\Omega}\mathbf j\cdot d\mathbf A.$ The divergence theorem gives the differential continuity equation, $\boxed{
  \frac{\partial\rho_q}{\partial t}
  +
  \boldsymbol{\nabla}\cdot\mathbf j
  =0
  }.$ In space-time notation, $\partial_\mu J^\mu=0.$

