p.src:
The structure of general relativity is now visible even before the field equation is written: $T_{\mu\nu}
  \longrightarrow
  \text{space-time curvature}
  \longrightarrow
  \text{geodesic motion}.$ Mass contributes because $E=mc^2$, but energy density is only one component of the source. Momentum density, energy flux, pressure, and shear must also contribute, because Lorentz transformations mix them.

