p.src:
Take the slow-motion, weak-field limit. The spatial components of $dx^\mu/d\tau$ are small compared with the time component, and $\frac{dt}{d\tau}\simeq1.$ For a spatial index $i$, the dominant term in the geodesic equation is $\frac{d^2x^i}{dt^2}
  \simeq
  -\Gamma^i{}_{00}.$

